    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span><span class=\"time\">25 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip warn\">Medium</span><span class=\"chip accent\">0/1 knapsack</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Counting DP</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/target-sum/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 494</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Target Sum</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Putting '+' or '-' in front of each number is the same as choosing the subset P that gets '+'. Two equations force sum(P) = (total + target) / 2, so the question becomes \"how many subsets have that sum?\": a 0/1 knapsack row of counts, walked downward. O(n * total) time, O(total) space.</p>\n"
  },
